cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "The Twilight of Antibiotics — Open Computational Companion"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic, reproducible dashboard companion to the paper
  "The Twilight of Antibiotics". Implements a closed-form super-exponential
  model of the antimicrobial-resistance (AMR) trajectory (1990–2060),
  SARIMA time-series forecasts, a carbapenem-resistance mortality spotlight,
  and an ESKAPEE pathogen × antibiotic map. All coefficients are embedded and
  hand-calibrated to published sources — no parameter fitting, no random
  sampling — so every figure is reproducible bit-for-bit.
